    "description": "Read, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write, Bash, WebFetch: Claude Code's built-in tools and which ones need approval in Manual mode, per the docs. Plus two limits and how to allow a command for good.",
    "companion_text": "More Claude workflows, step by step: follow Promptwerk. Based on the Claude Code docs (Tools reference, How Claude Code works), checked 2026-11-01. The terminal and editor are an animation, not a screen recording. Limits per the docs: the “Permission required” column applies to Manual mode and paths inside the working directory; outside it, Read, Grep and Glob ask too. Bash runs a built-in set of read-only commands without asking. On macOS, Linux and WSL, Grep and Glob are absent by default and Claude searches through Bash. In auto mode a classifier decides most prompts.",
